1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,083
Sweetheart, on Christmas morning in my house,

2
00:00:03,083 --> 00:00:05,412
nobody is allowed to open a single

3
00:00:05,412 --> 00:00:08,221
present until the cinnamon rolls come out

4
00:00:08,221 --> 00:00:09,044
of the oven.

5
00:00:09,224 --> 00:00:10,472
That's the rule,

6
00:00:10,472 --> 00:00:12,265
since nineteen seventy.

7
00:00:12,445 --> 00:00:14,684
The children sit on the stairs in

8
00:00:14,684 --> 00:00:18,077
their pajamas, smelling cinnamon and butter coming

9
00:00:18,077 --> 00:00:19,230
from the kitchen,

10
00:00:19,230 --> 00:00:22,147
and it's the longest twenty-five minutes of

11
00:00:22,147 --> 00:00:23,301
their whole year.

12
00:00:23,651 --> 00:00:26,543
But people tell me their cinnamon rolls

13
00:00:26,543 --> 00:00:28,174
come out hard and dry,

14
00:00:28,174 --> 00:00:29,583
or they never rise,

15
00:00:29,583 --> 00:00:31,956
or all the filling leaks out and

16
00:00:31,956 --> 00:00:33,217
burns on the pan.

17
00:00:33,397 --> 00:00:36,002
So tonight I'm giving you my overnight

18
00:00:36,002 --> 00:00:37,716
Christmas cinnamon rolls,

19
00:00:37,716 --> 00:00:40,322
every step, and the five mistakes that

20
00:00:40,322 --> 00:00:41,350
make them hard.

21
00:00:41,530 --> 00:00:42,713
And stay with me,

22
00:00:42,713 --> 00:00:45,217
because the last secret is the trick

23
00:00:45,217 --> 00:00:47,652
that lets you sleep in on Christmas

24
00:00:47,652 --> 00:00:49,947
morning and still have hot rolls.

25
00:00:50,298 --> 00:00:53,764
Grandma Pearl made cinnamon rolls every Saturday

26
00:00:53,764 --> 00:00:54,630
on the farm,

27
00:00:54,630 --> 00:00:56,652
in her big black wood stove,

28
00:00:56,652 --> 00:00:59,468
from a bread dough she'd started before

29
00:00:59,468 --> 00:00:59,829
dawn.

30
00:01:00,009 --> 00:01:01,948
She never measured anything.

31
00:01:02,128 --> 00:01:03,744
A handful of this,

32
00:01:03,744 --> 00:01:05,181
a pinch of that,

33
00:01:05,181 --> 00:01:07,875
and flour until it felt right.

34
00:01:08,055 --> 00:01:10,588
When I asked her for the recipe,

35
00:01:10,588 --> 00:01:11,934
she said, Ruthie,

36
00:01:11,934 --> 00:01:13,280
I can't tell you.

37
00:01:13,460 --> 00:01:14,764
My hands know it,

38
00:01:14,764 --> 00:01:16,606
and my hands can't talk.

39
00:01:16,956 --> 00:01:18,818
So the summer I was twelve,

40
00:01:18,818 --> 00:01:21,163
I stood next to her every Saturday

41
00:01:21,163 --> 00:01:23,163
with a pencil and a notebook,

42
00:01:23,163 --> 00:01:25,715
and every time she grabbed a handful,

43
00:01:25,715 --> 00:01:27,232
I made her put it in a

44
00:01:27,232 --> 00:01:28,612
measuring cup first.

45
00:01:28,792 --> 00:01:31,137
She grumbled the whole summer.

46
00:01:31,317 --> 00:01:32,726
But by September,

47
00:01:32,726 --> 00:01:34,881
I had it all written down.

48
00:01:35,061 --> 00:01:38,106
That notebook is in my kitchen drawer,

49
00:01:38,106 --> 00:01:40,669
with flour stains on every page.

50
00:01:41,019 --> 00:01:43,166
And here's the good news.

51
00:01:43,346 --> 00:01:45,674
Cinnamon rolls aren't hard,

52
00:01:45,674 --> 00:01:46,191
honey.

53
00:01:46,371 --> 00:01:48,228
They just take patience.

54
00:01:48,408 --> 00:01:50,306
Most of the time is the dough

55
00:01:50,306 --> 00:01:51,550
sitting and rising,

56
00:01:51,550 --> 00:01:53,644
and you're doing something else.

57
00:01:53,824 --> 00:01:55,976
In a minute I'll tell you the

58
00:01:55,976 --> 00:01:58,648
first mistake, and it happens in the

59
00:01:58,648 --> 00:02:00,206
first thirty seconds,

60
00:02:00,206 --> 00:02:02,358
before you even start mixing.

61
00:02:02,707 --> 00:02:05,512
Here's what you need for twelve big

62
00:02:05,512 --> 00:02:05,993
rolls.

63
00:02:06,173 --> 00:02:07,381
For the dough,

64
00:02:07,381 --> 00:02:09,192
one cup of warm milk.

65
00:02:09,372 --> 00:02:11,094
One packet of yeast,

66
00:02:11,094 --> 00:02:14,109
that's two and a quarter teaspoons.

67
00:02:14,289 --> 00:02:16,285
A quarter cup of sugar.

68
00:02:16,465 --> 00:02:17,348
One egg.

69
00:02:17,528 --> 00:02:19,504
A third of a cup of melted

70
00:02:19,504 --> 00:02:20,036
butter.

71
00:02:20,216 --> 00:02:22,247
One teaspoon of salt.

72
00:02:22,427 --> 00:02:24,821
And about three and a half cups

73
00:02:24,821 --> 00:02:25,516
of flour.

74
00:02:25,696 --> 00:02:26,906
For the filling,

75
00:02:26,906 --> 00:02:28,645
a stick of soft butter,

76
00:02:28,645 --> 00:02:30,915
one cup of packed brown sugar,

77
00:02:30,915 --> 00:02:33,335
and two tablespoons of cinnamon.

78
00:02:33,684 --> 00:02:35,216
And for the icing,

79
00:02:35,216 --> 00:02:37,598
four ounces of cream cheese,

80
00:02:37,598 --> 00:02:38,363
softened.

81
00:02:38,543 --> 00:02:40,784
A quarter cup of soft butter.

82
00:02:40,964 --> 00:02:43,337
One and a half cups of powdered

83
00:02:43,337 --> 00:02:43,797
sugar.

84
00:02:43,977 --> 00:02:46,055
A teaspoon of vanilla.

85
00:02:46,235 --> 00:02:47,919
And a splash of milk.

86
00:02:48,099 --> 00:02:51,288
Grandma Pearl used a simple powdered sugar

87
00:02:51,288 --> 00:02:54,250
glaze, but I started using cream cheese

88
00:02:54,250 --> 00:02:55,996
in nineteen eighty-two,

89
00:02:55,996 --> 00:02:58,351
and nobody in my family has let

90
00:02:58,351 --> 00:02:59,186
me go back.

91
00:02:59,536 --> 00:03:02,635
Step one, and here's mistake number one.

92
00:03:02,815 --> 00:03:04,568
Milk that's too hot.

93
00:03:04,748 --> 00:03:06,883
Hot milk kills the yeast,

94
00:03:06,883 --> 00:03:09,102
and your rolls never rise.

95
00:03:09,282 --> 00:03:11,843
Warm the milk until it's just warm,

96
00:03:11,843 --> 00:03:13,380
like a baby's bottle,

97
00:03:13,380 --> 00:03:15,575
about one hundred ten degrees.

98
00:03:15,755 --> 00:03:17,427
Put a drop on your wrist.

99
00:03:17,607 --> 00:03:19,332
It should feel warm,

100
00:03:19,332 --> 00:03:20,022
not hot.

101
00:03:20,202 --> 00:03:22,390
Stir in the yeast and a spoon

102
00:03:22,390 --> 00:03:23,371
of the sugar,

103
00:03:23,371 --> 00:03:25,031
and wait five minutes.

104
00:03:25,211 --> 00:03:27,231
It should get foamy on top.

105
00:03:27,581 --> 00:03:29,109
If it doesn't foam,

106
00:03:29,109 --> 00:03:31,683
honey, your yeast is old or your

107
00:03:31,683 --> 00:03:33,050
milk was too hot.

108
00:03:33,230 --> 00:03:35,134
Throw it out and start again.

109
00:03:35,314 --> 00:03:37,057
It's a quarter of a cup of

110
00:03:37,057 --> 00:03:37,392
milk.

111
00:03:37,572 --> 00:03:39,974
Better to lose that than three hours

112
00:03:39,974 --> 00:03:41,775
and a whole batch of dough.

113
00:03:41,955 --> 00:03:44,596
Then add the rest of the sugar,

114
00:03:44,596 --> 00:03:46,896
the egg, the melted butter,

115
00:03:46,896 --> 00:03:48,003
and the salt,

116
00:03:48,003 --> 00:03:48,770
and stir.

117
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:51,064
Now add the flour a cup at

118
00:03:51,064 --> 00:03:53,682
a time, mixing with a wooden spoon,

119
00:03:53,682 --> 00:03:55,551
until a soft dough forms.

120
00:03:55,731 --> 00:03:58,036
Turn it out on a floured counter

121
00:03:58,036 --> 00:04:00,630
and knead it for about five minutes,

122
00:04:00,630 --> 00:04:02,935
pushing it away with the heel of

123
00:04:02,935 --> 00:04:04,879
your hand, folding it back,

124
00:04:04,879 --> 00:04:05,960
and turning it.

125
00:04:06,140 --> 00:04:08,957
Mistake number two is adding too much

126
00:04:08,957 --> 00:04:09,414
flour.

127
00:04:09,594 --> 00:04:11,702
The dough should be soft and a

128
00:04:11,702 --> 00:04:13,952
little tacky, like the back of a

129
00:04:13,952 --> 00:04:14,795
sticky note.

130
00:04:14,975 --> 00:04:17,553
Too much flour makes hard rolls.

131
00:04:17,902 --> 00:04:19,500
If this is helping you,

132
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:21,861
honey, tap the like button for me.

133
00:04:22,041 --> 00:04:24,480
It helps Grandma more than you know.

134
00:04:24,660 --> 00:04:26,951
Put the dough in a buttered bowl,

135
00:04:26,951 --> 00:04:28,478
cover it with a towel,

136
00:04:28,478 --> 00:04:30,283
and set it somewhere warm,

137
00:04:30,283 --> 00:04:32,644
like on top of the refrigerator or

138
00:04:32,644 --> 00:04:34,796
in the oven with just the light

139
00:04:34,796 --> 00:04:35,004
on.

140
00:04:35,184 --> 00:04:37,529
Let it rise until it's doubled,

141
00:04:37,529 --> 00:04:39,647
about an hour to an hour and

142
00:04:39,647 --> 00:04:40,176
a half.

143
00:04:40,526 --> 00:04:42,591
And if your kitchen is cold,

144
00:04:42,591 --> 00:04:44,951
honey, like mine every December,

145
00:04:44,951 --> 00:04:47,458
here's how to help the dough rise.

146
00:04:47,638 --> 00:04:49,779
Turn the oven on to its lowest

147
00:04:49,779 --> 00:04:51,777
setting for just one minute,

148
00:04:51,777 --> 00:04:52,990
then turn it off.

149
00:04:53,170 --> 00:04:55,422
Put the bowl of dough inside with

150
00:04:55,422 --> 00:04:56,514
the door closed.

151
00:04:56,694 --> 00:04:58,921
It's warm and cozy in there,

152
00:04:58,921 --> 00:05:00,989
like a little bread hotel.

153
00:05:01,169 --> 00:05:03,890
Just don't forget it's there and turn

154
00:05:03,890 --> 00:05:05,581
the oven on to preheat.

155
00:05:05,761 --> 00:05:08,524
I did that once in nineteen ninety-one.

156
00:05:08,704 --> 00:05:10,016
The bowl melted.

157
00:05:10,366 --> 00:05:11,388
Step two.

158
00:05:11,568 --> 00:05:13,659
Punch the dough down gently,

159
00:05:13,659 --> 00:05:15,749
and roll it out on a floured

160
00:05:15,749 --> 00:05:17,915
counter into a big rectangle,

161
00:05:17,915 --> 00:05:20,229
about sixteen by twelve inches.

162
00:05:20,409 --> 00:05:23,176
Spread the soft butter all over it,

163
00:05:23,176 --> 00:05:24,679
right to the edges,

164
00:05:24,679 --> 00:05:27,209
except leave one long edge bare,

165
00:05:27,209 --> 00:05:28,316
about an inch.

166
00:05:28,496 --> 00:05:31,200
Then mix the brown sugar and cinnamon,

167
00:05:31,200 --> 00:05:33,976
and sprinkle it evenly over the butter.

168
00:05:34,156 --> 00:05:36,431
Press it in lightly with your hand.

169
00:05:36,780 --> 00:05:39,746
Mistake number three is melted butter in

170
00:05:39,746 --> 00:05:40,635
the filling.

171
00:05:40,815 --> 00:05:43,666
Melted butter runs out the sides while

172
00:05:43,666 --> 00:05:46,216
it bakes, and takes the sugar with

173
00:05:46,216 --> 00:05:48,242
it, and it all burns on the

174
00:05:48,242 --> 00:05:49,592
bottom of the pan.

175
00:05:49,772 --> 00:05:51,186
Use soft butter,

176
00:05:51,186 --> 00:05:52,512
like for toast.

177
00:05:52,692 --> 00:05:55,594
It holds the cinnamon sugar in place,

178
00:05:55,594 --> 00:05:58,495
and it melts slowly inside the rolls,

179
00:05:58,495 --> 00:06:01,945
into that gooey swirl everybody fights over.

180
00:06:02,296 --> 00:06:03,463
Now roll it up,

181
00:06:03,463 --> 00:06:06,266
starting from the long side with the

182
00:06:06,266 --> 00:06:08,601
filling, toward the bare edge,

183
00:06:08,601 --> 00:06:09,691
nice and snug.

184
00:06:09,871 --> 00:06:12,065
Pinch the bare edge to seal it.

185
00:06:12,245 --> 00:06:14,858
Then cut it into twelve rolls.

186
00:06:15,038 --> 00:06:17,325
And here's my favorite trick.

187
00:06:17,505 --> 00:06:18,968
Don't use a knife.

188
00:06:19,148 --> 00:06:21,946
Use a piece of plain dental floss.

189
00:06:22,126 --> 00:06:24,062
Slide it under the log,

190
00:06:24,062 --> 00:06:26,418
cross the ends over the top,

191
00:06:26,418 --> 00:06:27,176
and pull.

192
00:06:27,356 --> 00:06:30,171
It cuts a perfect round roll without

193
00:06:30,171 --> 00:06:31,187
squashing it.

194
00:06:31,538 --> 00:06:34,075
Put the rolls in a buttered nine

195
00:06:34,075 --> 00:06:35,344
by thirteen pan,

196
00:06:35,344 --> 00:06:36,296
cut side up,

197
00:06:36,296 --> 00:06:37,802
three rows of four,

198
00:06:37,802 --> 00:06:40,419
with a little space between them.

199
00:06:40,599 --> 00:06:43,492
They'll grow together as they rise and

200
00:06:43,492 --> 00:06:43,873
bake.

201
00:06:44,053 --> 00:06:45,853
And here's the next part.

202
00:06:46,033 --> 00:06:48,286
So far, warm milk not hot,

203
00:06:48,286 --> 00:06:49,412
a soft dough,

204
00:06:49,412 --> 00:06:51,752
soft butter in the filling,

205
00:06:51,752 --> 00:06:54,438
rolled snug and cut with floss.

206
00:06:54,618 --> 00:06:56,442
Now the secret I promised,

207
00:06:56,442 --> 00:06:57,985
for Christmas morning.

208
00:06:58,336 --> 00:07:01,145
Instead of letting them rise and baking

209
00:07:01,145 --> 00:07:02,298
them right away,

210
00:07:02,298 --> 00:07:05,180
cover the pan tightly with plastic wrap,

211
00:07:05,180 --> 00:07:07,126
and put it in the icebox on

212
00:07:07,126 --> 00:07:08,134
Christmas Eve.

213
00:07:08,314 --> 00:07:11,163
The cold slows the yeast way down,

214
00:07:11,163 --> 00:07:14,011
and the rolls rise very slowly all

215
00:07:14,011 --> 00:07:14,514
night.

216
00:07:14,694 --> 00:07:17,023
You can leave them in the icebox

217
00:07:17,023 --> 00:07:18,769
for up to sixteen hours.

218
00:07:18,949 --> 00:07:20,075
That's the secret.

219
00:07:20,255 --> 00:07:22,364
All the work is done the night

220
00:07:22,364 --> 00:07:22,856
before.

221
00:07:23,206 --> 00:07:24,625
On Christmas morning,

222
00:07:24,625 --> 00:07:26,450
take the pan out and set it

223
00:07:26,450 --> 00:07:29,356
on the counter for about forty-five minutes

224
00:07:29,356 --> 00:07:30,100
to an hour,

225
00:07:30,100 --> 00:07:32,533
until the rolls are puffy and almost

226
00:07:32,533 --> 00:07:33,074
doubled.

227
00:07:33,254 --> 00:07:36,499
Mistake number four is baking them straight

228
00:07:36,499 --> 00:07:37,706
from the icebox,

229
00:07:37,706 --> 00:07:38,084
cold.

230
00:07:38,264 --> 00:07:40,156
They come out dense and heavy in

231
00:07:40,156 --> 00:07:40,806
the middle.

232
00:07:40,986 --> 00:07:43,099
Give them time to wake up,

233
00:07:43,099 --> 00:07:43,587
honey.

234
00:07:43,767 --> 00:07:46,004
Put on the coffee and the carols

235
00:07:46,004 --> 00:07:47,122
while they rise.

236
00:07:47,473 --> 00:07:50,225
Bake them at three hundred fifty degrees

237
00:07:50,225 --> 00:07:52,772
for twenty-two to twenty-six minutes,

238
00:07:52,772 --> 00:07:55,112
until they're golden brown on top.

239
00:07:55,292 --> 00:07:57,625
And mistake number five.

240
00:07:57,805 --> 00:07:59,442
Overbaking them.

241
00:07:59,622 --> 00:08:02,720
That's the main reason cinnamon rolls come

242
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:03,384
out hard.

243
00:08:03,564 --> 00:08:05,753
The centers should be just done,

244
00:08:05,753 --> 00:08:08,352
at about one hundred ninety degrees if

245
00:08:08,352 --> 00:08:09,857
you use a thermometer.

246
00:08:10,037 --> 00:08:11,955
If the tops brown too fast,

247
00:08:11,955 --> 00:08:13,944
lay a piece of foil over the

248
00:08:13,944 --> 00:08:16,004
pan for the last ten minutes.

249
00:08:16,355 --> 00:08:17,763
While they bake,

250
00:08:17,763 --> 00:08:19,083
make the icing.

251
00:08:19,263 --> 00:08:21,899
Beat the soft cream cheese and butter

252
00:08:21,899 --> 00:08:23,466
together until smooth.

253
00:08:23,646 --> 00:08:26,077
Add the powdered sugar and vanilla,

254
00:08:26,077 --> 00:08:27,605
and beat until fluffy.

255
00:08:27,785 --> 00:08:29,786
Add a little milk if it's too

256
00:08:29,786 --> 00:08:30,200
thick.

257
00:08:30,380 --> 00:08:32,560
Then when the rolls come out,

258
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:34,890
let them cool for five minutes,

259
00:08:34,890 --> 00:08:37,597
and spread the icing over them while

260
00:08:37,597 --> 00:08:40,153
they're warm, so it melts into all

261
00:08:40,153 --> 00:08:40,979
the swirls.

262
00:08:41,330 --> 00:08:43,490
And then I ring the little brass

263
00:08:43,490 --> 00:08:45,583
bell from Grandma Pearl's farm,

264
00:08:45,583 --> 00:08:48,148
and the children come running down the

265
00:08:48,148 --> 00:08:48,621
stairs.

266
00:08:48,801 --> 00:08:49,917
One roll each,

267
00:08:49,917 --> 00:08:51,192
a glass of milk,

268
00:08:51,192 --> 00:08:53,105
and then, and only then,

269
00:08:53,105 --> 00:08:54,141
the presents.

270
00:08:54,321 --> 00:08:56,732
My grandson is thirty-four now,

271
00:08:56,732 --> 00:08:59,221
honey, with children of his own.

272
00:08:59,401 --> 00:09:01,789
And he still sits on the stairs

273
00:09:01,789 --> 00:09:03,638
and waits for that bell.

274
00:09:03,989 --> 00:09:06,504
Cinnamon rolls are best the day they're

275
00:09:06,504 --> 00:09:08,826
made, but they keep two days covered

276
00:09:08,826 --> 00:09:09,794
on the counter.

277
00:09:09,974 --> 00:09:12,746
Warm one in the microwave for fifteen

278
00:09:12,746 --> 00:09:14,919
seconds, and it's soft again.

279
00:09:15,099 --> 00:09:17,221
And they freeze beautifully,

280
00:09:17,221 --> 00:09:17,979
unfrosted.

281
00:09:18,159 --> 00:09:20,826
Wrap them tight and freeze them for

282
00:09:20,826 --> 00:09:21,665
two months.

283
00:09:21,845 --> 00:09:23,438
Thaw them overnight,

284
00:09:23,438 --> 00:09:25,190
warm them in the oven,

285
00:09:25,190 --> 00:09:26,384
and frost them.

286
00:09:26,564 --> 00:09:28,560
A pan of frozen rolls is the

287
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:30,698
best present for a new mother.

288
00:09:31,048 --> 00:09:32,348
So one more time.

289
00:09:32,528 --> 00:09:34,223
Warm milk, not hot,

290
00:09:34,223 --> 00:09:36,185
and wait for the foam.

291
00:09:36,365 --> 00:09:38,315
A soft, tacky dough,

292
00:09:38,315 --> 00:09:40,754
don't add too much flour.

293
00:09:40,934 --> 00:09:43,070
Soft butter in the filling,

294
00:09:43,070 --> 00:09:43,941
not melted.

295
00:09:44,121 --> 00:09:46,540
Roll it snug and cut it with

296
00:09:46,540 --> 00:09:47,058
floss.

297
00:09:47,238 --> 00:09:50,129
Into the icebox on Christmas Eve.

298
00:09:50,309 --> 00:09:52,005
Let them wake up an hour in

299
00:09:52,005 --> 00:09:52,758
the morning.

300
00:09:52,938 --> 00:09:55,133
Bake them just until golden,

301
00:09:55,133 --> 00:09:56,700
and frost them warm.

302
00:09:56,880 --> 00:09:59,901
That's Grandma Pearl's cinnamon rolls,

303
00:09:59,901 --> 00:10:01,571
written down at last.

304
00:10:01,921 --> 00:10:04,221
Tell me in the comments,

305
00:10:04,221 --> 00:10:05,276
sweetheart.

306
00:10:05,456 --> 00:10:08,170
What does your family eat on Christmas

307
00:10:08,170 --> 00:10:08,741
morning?

308
00:10:08,921 --> 00:10:11,487
Cinnamon rolls, a casserole,

309
00:10:11,487 --> 00:10:12,312
pancakes?

310
00:10:12,492 --> 00:10:14,071
I'd love to know.

311
00:10:14,251 --> 00:10:17,413
The whole playlist of Grandma's recipes is

312
00:10:17,413 --> 00:10:19,446
right there on your screen,

313
00:10:19,446 --> 00:10:21,554
and I'll see you in the next

314
00:10:21,554 --> 00:10:22,006
video.

315
00:10:22,186 --> 00:10:23,765
Good night, honey.

316
00:10:23,945 --> 00:10:25,396
Merry Christmas.
